What:		/proc/subsys_sleepmon/adsp
What:		/proc/subsys_sleepmon/adsp_compact
What:		/proc/subsys_sleepmon/cdsp
What:		/proc/subsys_sleepmon/cdsp_compact
What:		/proc/subsys_sleepmon/slpi
What:		/proc/subsys_sleepmon/slpi_compact
Date:		January 2024
Contact:	OPLUS power-management maintainers
Description:
		Read-only snapshots of Qualcomm subsystem low-power votes. The
		unqualified files provide a human-readable report. The `_compact`
		files provide the key/value form consumed by ColorOS power
		diagnostics, including the selected sleep mode, rejection reasons,
		XO voters, active DSP thread, latency and duration voters, and
		disabled LPRM resources.

		ADSP uses Qualcomm SMEM host 2, SLPI/SSC host 3, and CDSP host 5.
		The firmware-owned tables are SMEM items 590 and 591. Reads fail
		cleanly when either table is absent, too small, or reports counts
		outside the 9R layout; the kernel never modifies those tables.
